              text: 'Step : Place the two sets of ice cream sticks, as indicated in the figure. Step : Using a rubber band, attach the ice cream spoon, as shown in the figure. Your catapult is now ready. Figure 3.4: Steps for making a catapult using ice cream sticks and spoon Makers Skill.indd_July 11.indd Kaushal Bodh Grade Working Model of Robotic Arm Materials : You will need ice cream sticks, glue, old bottle caps, toothpicks, and a cutter. Step : Pierce the ice cream sticks in the centre. Break a toothpick into small pieces and join the ice cream sticks by passing this piece through the holes. Remember to add glue where the sticks are joined. Step : Join a few more ice cream sticks just like in Step 1. There needs to be a free movement of the ice cream sticks. Step : Cut out the centres of the bottle caps with the cutter so that you end up with two circular shapes. Step : Glue the bottle caps to the ends of the first set of ice cream sticks. Your robotic arm is ready. Figure 3.5: Steps for making a robotic arm using ice cream sticks, bottle caps and toothpicks Makers Skill.indd_July 11.indd Maker Skills 1. Draw a sketch of the toy, giving accurate measurements where different parts are connected. You can paste a photogr aph of the toy in the space given below: 2. Write down instructions for someone who is using robotic arm for the first time. ................................................................................................................. ................................................................................................................. ....................... .......................................................................................... Activity 3: Using a propeller to make toys A propeller is a wheel with blades.',
